
### AI-Powered Fact-Checking Assistant using LangGraph

Developed an intelligent fact-checking assistant that leverages Agentic AI workflows to verify user claims using real-time web evidence. The application classifies incoming queries as either casual conversations or fact-checking requests and dynamically routes them through specialized workflows using LangGraph's conditional graph architecture.

For fact-checking tasks, the assistant retrieves relevant information from trusted web sources, analyzes the collected evidence using a Large Language Model, and generates a concise verification report. The system also maintains conversational memory to provide context-aware interactions across multiple turns.

Built with a user-friendly Gradio chat interface, the project demonstrates practical implementation of LLM orchestration, tool integration, memory management, and multi-step reasoning in real-world AI applications.

### Key Features

* 🔹 Intelligent query classification (Casual Chat vs. Fact Check)
* 🔹 Conditional routing using LangGraph
* 🔹 Real-time web evidence retrieval
* 🔹 LLM-powered claim verification and reasoning
* 🔹 Multi-turn conversation memory
* 🔹 Interactive Gradio chat interface
* 🔹 Modular and scalable agent architecture

